-- title:
--   A good point lies on no other Igusa branch (q=2)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with the hypothesis `hq2` that $q=2$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `hA : A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a nonunit of $A$. The following groups of data and hypotheses are in force.
--
--   *Supersingular places.* A finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, with `hW` saying that $W$ consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, that is of the places $w$ which are rational (the structure map from the base field onto the residue field of $w$ is surjective), are affine geometric places, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen})\in \mathrm{ssJSet}\,q$, the set of $j$-invariants all of whose elliptic curves have trivial $q$-torsion group in the sense of `ssJSet`.
--
--   *Fields and constant reduction.* The hypothesis `hle` that $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ inside the Laurent series field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; a `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ (a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of the former, a surjective reduction map onto the latter with kernel the maximal ideal, extending reduction of constants, together with a place map preserving degrees and compatible with divisors); and `hR₀`, which requires that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in the Laurent series field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, this image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   *Igusa branches.* An index $\zeta$ of a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and a family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ indexed by the projective line $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$, subject to: `hIg_inf`, that $f \in O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ if and only if there are Laurent series $x,y$ with coefficients in $A$ such that the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ is nonzero and $f$ times the image of $y$ equals the image of $x$ (the Gauss ring description of the branch at infinity); `hIg`, that each line $\ell$ is $\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma \cdot \mathrm{lineInfty}\,q$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the preimage of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ under $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$; `hIg_inj`, injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; and `hIg_perm`, that for every index $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the automorphism $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ permutes the family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$.
--
--   *Supersingular valuation rings.* A family $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ indexed by $W$, subject to four hypotheses: `hSS_A`, that a constant from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ exactly when it lies in $A$; `hSS_over`, that for $s \in W$ and $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ which is regular at every place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ at which the element given by the $q$-expansion of $j$ is regular, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and, for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $f$, the difference of that image and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$; `hSS_fix`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is preserved by every $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ contains an element $t$ such that $t - a$ is a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every $a \in A$.
--
--   *Regular prolongation.* A `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ from $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ to $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,(q^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$ (a valuation subring with surjective residue map onto that field, kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with constants and with a nonvanishing-scaling property), together with `hR` identifying $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$, and `hR₀O` stating that $f$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if its image lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$.
--
--   *Ramification and descent data.* An element $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$; an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$ such that $A \cap k_0$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ and algebraically closed residue field, plus `hκ`: every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. Further, a prime $\ell \ge 3$ with $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally a finite extension $K_1$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and a valuation subring $A_1$ of $K_1$ cut out by $A$, which is a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   With $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the assertion quantifies over every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $k_0$ satisfying: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is everything; $F_0$ is stable under every $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; a linear-disjointness condition, namely that for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $K'$-linearly independent family $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every family $a$ of elements of $T' := k_0(\text{image of } K') \sqcup F_0$ with $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$, all $a_i$ vanish; and $F_0$ contains every element of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ whose Laurent series lies in the image of $\mathrm{coeffEmb}$ (the rational $q$-expansions).
--
--   Write $T_1 := \mathrm{adjoin}_{k_0}(\text{image of } K_1) \sqcup F_0$. The assertion further quantifies over an $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ whose structure map agrees with the inclusion $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ on elements of $A_1$; over a nonzero $j_1 \in T_1$ whose image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ is the inclusion of the element of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ given by $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,\mathrm{jq}$; and over a finite set $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of places of $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,(q^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$ for which there exists a ring homomorphism $j$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ to that field such that every $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ has its image in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with $R$-residue equal to $j$ of its $R_0$-residue, and such that $Q \in N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ if and only if there is $s \in W$ with $g$ in the valuation subring of $s$ exactly when $j(g)$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$.
--
--   On the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak X_1 := \mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}\,A_1\,T_1\,j_1$ — the pushout of the two affine charts $\mathrm{XFin} = \operatorname{Spec}\mathrm{chartAlgFin}$ and $\mathrm{XInf} = \operatorname{Spec}\mathrm{chartAlgInf}$, where $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}$, respectively $\mathrm{chartAlgInf}$, is the subalgebra of elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$, respectively over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$ — four predicates are introduced. For $x \in \mathfrak X_1$ and $f \in T_1$, $\mathrm{InStalk}\,x\,f$ says that for every point $y$ of either chart mapping to $x$ there are chart elements $g,h$ with $h \notin y$ and $f h = g$; $\mathrm{InMax}\,x\,f$ is the same with the extra requirement $g \in y$. For a place $P$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $\mathrm{Centred}\,P\,x$ says that $P$ is rational and that every $f$ with $\mathrm{InStalk}\,x\,f$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$, has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and satisfies $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ less than $1$ if and only if $\mathrm{InMax}\,x\,f$. For $Q$ a place of $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,(q^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$, $\mathrm{Reads}\,x\,Q$ says that every $f$ with $\mathrm{InStalk}\,x\,f$ has its image in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, with $R$-residue in the valuation subring of $Q$ and a nonunit there exactly when $\mathrm{InMax}\,x\,f$. The predicates $\mathrm{Centred}$ and $\mathrm{Reads}$ are introduced as abbreviations and do not occur in the conclusion.
--
--   Finally, $\mathrm{GoodPt}\,x$ is the conjunction of: the structure morphism $\mathrm{toBase}$ sends $x$ to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$; every $y$ to which $x$ specialises equals $x$; for every point $y$ of the finite chart over $x$, every chart element whose image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ is a nonunit of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ lies in $y$; the same for the chart at infinity; and, for every point $y$ of the finite chart over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}$ to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(\mathrm{jChartFin})$ does not lie in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\Omega$.
--
--   The conclusion asserts: for every point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ with $\mathrm{GoodPt}\,x$, the predicate $\mathrm{OffBranch}\,x$ holds, namely for every line $\ell \in \mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ with $\ell \ne \mathrm{lineInfty}\,q$ both of the following hold: for every point $y$ of the finite chart mapping to $x$ there is an element $b$ of $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}$ whose image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ is a nonunit of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ and which does not lie in $y$; and for every point $y$ of the chart at infinity mapping to $x$ there is an element $b$ of $\mathrm{chartAlgInf}$ whose image is a nonunit of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ and which does not lie in $y$.
--
--   This is the separation statement for the Igusa branches at the prime $q=2$: a closed point of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model which is non-supersingular and lies on the branch at infinity is exhibited, chart by chart, as lying off every other Igusa branch $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$. It is the $q=2$ counterpart of the corresponding statement for $q \ge 5$, and is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_goodPt_and_offBranch_and_reads_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_goodPt_and_offBranch_and_reads_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_two) in the construction of the semistable covering of the modular curve of full level $q^2M'$.
